        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 2 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## a.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"age\", \"id\"), Documented = c(\"yes\", \n\"yes\"), Label = c(\"Age in years\", \"Participant id\"), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(\"age\", \n\"id\"), Source = c(\"codebook_a.csv\", \"codebook_a.csv\"), Status = c(\"labelled\", \n\"labelled\")), row.names = 1:2, class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Documented but Unused Variables\n\n1 documented variable was not matched to any data column.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Variable = \"income\", Label = \"Annual income\", \n    Source = \"codebook_a.csv\"), row.names = 3L, class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Scales",
          "Scale naming from the manuscript needs an LLM (enable with `llm_use(TRUE)`); the dictionary rules matcher still names instruments whose abbreviation matches a known scale."
        ]
